## The design

**Concept: a technical datasheet.** Not the usual dark-mode dev-docs template — warm paper stock (`#f2efe6`) with a fine multiply-blend grain, ink-red accent (`#b8371f`), hairline rules, and numbered sections (`§00`…`§05`). Monospace carries every piece of structure (nav numbers, labels, chips, table headers, flags); Instrument Serif carries the voice (headline, section titles, error messages). The only dark surfaces on the page are the terminal blocks — so your eye goes straight to the commands.

**Section order** — install-first, because that's what a homepage visitor came for:

| | |
|---|---|
| §00 Overview | Hero: "A markdown build tool that does *one thing*." + a 4-cell fact grid (version / licence / Node 20+ / plugin resolution: none) |
| §01 Install | Four tabs, sliding into a connected terminal panel, copy button top-right |
| §02 Quickstart | The block verbatim, then the how-it-works prose |
| §03 Configuration | Real table — key / type pill / default / description |
| §04 Commands | Two-up card grid, `$` prompt prefix, flags as bordered chips |
| §05 Errors | Accent-barred cards: code chip, message in serif, fix below |

**Navigation** is a sticky left rail with a live scroll-spy via `IntersectionObserver` (top-third of viewport wins) — the active item turns red with an underline that draws in. Under 900px it collapses into a horizontal pill scroller docked beneath the masthead.

**Requirements kept intact:** all four installers with exact commands, arrow-key-navigable tabs and a working `navigator.clipboard` copy with "Copied" feedback; quickstart string untouched; all six config keys with type/default/description; all four commands with every flag; all three errors with message and fix; all four footer links. The `data-install` / `data-config` / `data-cmd` / `data-error` hooks are preserved.

Also tightened the original behaviour slightly: the copy timeout is now cleared on unmount and on re-click, so rapid clicks don't reset the label early.
